select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'calendars', 'chapter', 'requests-offers-and-bookings', 'The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.

## The master calendar

1. Move through time with the arrows and **Today**, or pick a date.
2. Choose the range: **Today**, **Week**, **2 weeks** or **Month**. **Agenda** shows a list instead.
3. The legend: confirmed, on rent, request, offer, not blocking, placeholder, block, Turo and dates taken.
4. Each row is a car, with its photo, code and plate. Bars are bookings and blocks in the Now view''s colours (out red, booked black); the red line is now and today is the black day at the top. Bookings that hold the car run along the top; requests, offers, bookings that do not block and placeholders run underneath. Bars for the same days sit one under the other, never on top of each other.
5. A bar with a red ring and **!** has its dates taken: a request or offer over a booked car or a block. Open it to see what it clashes with, then offer another car or other dates. A placeholder (dashed grey) never clashes with anything.

![](/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/calendar; pins: 1 23.6 20.0, 2 47.9 20.0, 3 38.9 31.4, 4 62.5 44.7")

6. Tap a bar for its details in a side panel (on a phone it opens from the bottom). On a phone the calendar opens on **Agenda**: the bookings and blocks by day, each with the car''s photo, the times and its status.

## Move a booking, add or remove a block

1. To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press **Confirm the move**.
2. To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press **Create the block**. **New block** at the top does the same.
3. To remove a block, open it and press **Remove the block**.

> Tip: After every confirmed trip a cleaning block holds the car for its turnaround time. It follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Remove it from the side panel if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.

## A car''s own calendar

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Calendar tab.

1. The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.
2. Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press **Change** to give this car its own time.

![](/guides/img/admin-07-vehicle-calendar-desktop-98586ca8.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles/b37ead6c-6196-4cd6-92ff-a14a55a8d5f2?tab=calendar; pins: 1 46.5 35.5, 2 50.1 46.2")
', 'Calendars', 'The master calendar, moving bookings, blocks, cleaning time and a car''s calendar.',
  'The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.

## Which cars are free (release 44)

At the top of **Calendar**: choose the **Pickup** and the **Return** the customer wants and you see every car at once.

1. Each car says **Available** (green edge) or **Not available** (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the **Next free** start for the same length of rental.
2. An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.
3. Narrow it with **Class**, **Seats at least** and **Price a day up to**, or tick **Available only**.
4. Press **Offer these dates** on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.
5. No customer''s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.

## The master calendar

1. Move through time with the arrows and **Today**, or pick a date.
2. Choose the range: **Today**, **Week**, **2 weeks** or **Month**. **Agenda** shows a list instead.
3. The legend: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance (blue stripes), not blocking, placeholder, block, Turo and dates taken.
4. Each row is a car, with its photo, code and plate. Bars are bookings and blocks in the Now view''s colours (out red, booked black); the red line is now and today is the black day at the top. Bookings that hold the car run along the top; requests, offers, bookings that do not block and placeholders run underneath. Bars for the same days sit one under the other, never on top of each other.
5. A bar with a red ring and **!** has its dates taken: a request or offer over a booked car or a block. Open it to see what it clashes with, then offer another car or other dates. A placeholder (dashed grey) never clashes with anything.

![](/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/calendar; pins: 1 23.6 20.0, 2 47.9 20.0, 3 38.9 31.4, 4 62.5 44.7")

6. Tap a bar for its details in a side panel (on a phone it opens from the bottom). On a phone the calendar opens on **Agenda**: the bookings and blocks by day, each with the car''s photo, the times and its status.

## Move a booking, add or remove a block

1. To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press **Confirm the move**.
2. To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press **Create the block**. **New block** at the top does the same.
3. To remove a block, open it and press **Remove the block**.

> Tip: After every confirmed trip a cleaning block holds the car for its turnaround time. It follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Remove it from the side panel if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.

## A car''s own calendar

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Calendar tab.

1. The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.
2. Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press **Change** to give this car its own time.

