ass="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To use the phone&#39;s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-carmacars-app-links" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The CarmaCars app links</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see <b class="gd-ui">Download the CarmaCars app</b> in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder&#39;s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, <b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-minimize-the-pop-up-and-the-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Minimize the pop-up, and the Call helper (release 43)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The line at the top right of a call minimizes it to a small chip at the bottom of the page: the caller&#39;s name and the call&#39;s timer. A click anywhere outside the panel, or Esc, minimizes it too; nothing is closed by accident. Press the chip to open the call again. The cross still closes a call in this browser, and a new call always opens by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Inside each call, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> is for new hires: <b class="gd-ui">Say</b> (the greeting, with the staff member&#39;s first name and the caller&#39;s name and booking when known), a button for each situation with 3 to 6 short steps and links to the right page of their portal, and <b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> puts it away in that browser.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You write all of it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> (see Settings). <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on the helper takes you there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter page has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal&#39;s renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-call-button-through-twilio-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call button through Twilio (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Since release 44 calls are made and taken in the browser (below); ringing the staff member&#39;s own cell first is a Program setting, off by default. The release 35 way: <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a staff page rings the staff member&#39;s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo and says why. A staff member with no mobile on their profile is asked for it the first time they press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> (a Canadian or US mobile, saved without a texted code), then the call starts (release 40).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-in-the-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in the browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff, Admins included, make and take calls in the browser of the staff and Admin portals, with the CarmaCars number as caller ID. Staff abroad never use their own international number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> anywhere opens a bar at the bottom left of the page: <b class="gd-ui">Calling ...</b>, then the timer, <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Hang up</b>. The browser asks once for the microphone. The call is kept on the person&#39;s history with its length and its recording, as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the business number rings the browsers of the staff who have a staff page open, by role (customer service and Sales by default), each with <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Sales sees the caller&#39;s name or the number hidden.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online or nobody answered: the caller hears the message of Program settings and it is a missed call with its task and its text back, like every missed call. With a forward number set, the call goes there instead. Never to a staff member&#39;s own number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, the phone settings: <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser</b> (on), Whose browser rings (cs, sales; add admin, fleet or finance), <b class="gd-ui">Ring for (seconds)</b> (25), Nobody answered: forward to (empty), <b class="gd-ui">Nobody answered: the message</b>, and Ring my own mobile first (the release 35 way, off).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Setting up Twilio once: save the GitHub repository secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID (AC...), TWILIO_API_KEY (an API key SID, SK...), TWILIO_API_SECRET (that key&#39;s secret) and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN (the account&#39;s Auth Token, which checks every request from Twilio), and TWILIO_CALLER_ID (the business number, for example +12895550123) when it differs from the CarmaCars number of Site settings. The business number must be a Twilio number or a verified caller ID in Twilio. The site makes the TwiML App &quot;CarmaCars browser calls&quot; itself, and points a Twilio business number with no Voice URL at the site. For incoming calls to ring browsers, calls to the business number must reach that Twilio number (buy it in Twilio, or forward to it). Until all is set, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> says what is missing.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, <b class="gd-ui">Reveal</b> shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b> (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call back</b> opens the conversation; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered SLA minutes</b>) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-recording-and-transcripts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call recording and transcripts (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded from the moment the customer answers. No caller notice plays.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The recording is copied to CarmaCars&#39; private storage and deleted at Twilio once our copy is safe (Program settings, on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">It is turned into text with the free daily AI allowance; when the allowance is used, the call waits for the next day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript, its summary and Play recording show on the renter&#39;s, the lead&#39;s, the booking&#39;s and the conversation&#39;s history, for Admins, customer service and Sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript feeds the renter&#39;s and the lead&#39;s intent at once (hot, warm or cold, with what they said they want).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Recording and deleting at Twilio are two switches in Program settings, under the phone settings.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'hiring', 'chapter', 'referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage', 'Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role''s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.

## Open a role and send the apply link

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links.

1. Press **Open the role** to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); **Close the role** takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.
2. Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.
3. Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role''s questions, about five minutes.
4. **Pass mark and pay** changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.

## What happens to each application

The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.

- Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).
- Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so.
- Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.
- A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.
- Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.

## Review the applications

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Applications.

1. Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.
2. **Invite anyway** sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. **Decline** sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).
3. A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.

## Interview days

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Interview days.

1. Press **Add an interview day**: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).
2. Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate''s email and on their page.
3. Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.
4. **Turn off** stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.

## Run the calls with the rubric

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Calls.

1. Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press **Start**.
2. The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.
3. Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press **Save the rubric**. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.

## Shortlist and Hire

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Shortlist.

1. Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.
2. Open the candidate and press **Hire**. A short form opens: the **Role** (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the **Start date** and the **Pay**, filled in with the role''s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.
3. Press **Confirm: hire and start onboarding**. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do''s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email; their call slot and AI interview link close.
4. The **Onboarding** card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire''s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press **Send the agreement**. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press **Verify**. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.
5. **Not hired** closes a candidate after the call without an email; **Withdrawn** is for one who no longer wants the role.

> Good to know: Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.


> Good to know: A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows "N applicants invited but no interview day is open for" the role, with **Add an interview day**. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time ("No call times are open right now"), get "New times are open" when the day is added.

## Decisions and the emails they send

The rubric''s **Decision** is Hire, Maybe, No, **Good fit for Sales instead** or No show. Recording one sends nothing.

1. **Good fit for Sales instead** refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.
2. Open **Hiring**, **Emails to send**: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.
3. **Change** a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or **Undo** it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).
4. Press **Send all decision emails**. Choose **Now**, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press **Hire** on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.

## AI interviews for the remote roles

Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. **People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: **Turn off** sends the remote roles the booking link again. **Interview settings**: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).

1. The candidate gets one email, **Start my interview**. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.
2. They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role''s rubric: experience, the role''s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role''s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Every answer is on video and spoken, nothing is typed, and the English question is spoken too. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.
3. When the last answer is in, the candidate is **Interviewed**. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, scores every answer out of 10 with a one-line reason, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: **Invite to a live call**, **Hire**, **Decline** or **Good fit for Sales instead**. Hiring shows "N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision".
4. Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript, the AI''s score for that rubric line and the answer''s score out of 10. **Watch all** plays every video one after the other.
5. The interview decides by itself (release 41): a pass needs all of these: the score at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in **Interview settings**), no knock-out answer, the answers averaging 7 or more out of 10 with none under 5, and spoken English judged good or fluent. A Sales applicant who passes is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy. Every other role that passes (customer service, fleet, finance and field) is invited to book an interview date. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press **Invite to a live call** on any candidate.
6. A link that expired: **New interview link** emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.

> Good to know: You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. **Interview settings** holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and **Decide by hand** if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings > Usage, "Hiring interviews"); when today''s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.

## Redo the AI interview

If an interview went badly for a reason that is not the applicant''s (a broken camera, a lost connection), open the candidate and press **Redo the AI interview**, then confirm.

1. Their staff access ends if they were already hired.
2. The old interview and its answers are kept as history on the candidate.
3. The application goes back to **Invited** and a new interview link is emailed, good for 7 days.

A redone interview follows the same pass rule as any other: only a Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself.

## Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed

- The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day''s **How** is only the default shown.
- Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with **Confirm my call** (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.
- **Calls** shows **Confirmed**, **Waiting** or **Asked 24 hours before** for each remote call, and **Cancelled: not confirmed** for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.

## Hire from any stage (release 35)
**Hire** is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: "<name> hired as <role>, starts <date>, training not started", which opens their academy progress.

## Every applicant into Sales

1. A closed role''s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.
2. The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.
3. Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.
4. A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview''s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.
5. The Hire form''s standard pay reads the role''s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.

## In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)

An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).

1. An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.
2. The list and the candidate page show **Lives in**, flag **Location mismatch** when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer **Move to Remote Sales** to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.
3. **Hire** chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.

## Interview dates before the townhall (release 35, widened in release 43)

Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 12:00 to 13:00), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on **Calls** here and on the Fleet home page.

## Interview call reminders (release 41)

For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day''s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or **Call** for a phone call). **Today** shows **Interviews today**: each call''s time, candidate, role and its **Join** or **Call** button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.', 'Hiring', 'Open roles and apply links for Indeed and OnlineJobs.ph, the applications and their scores, AI interviews for the remote roles, interview days, the rubric during each call, the ranked shortlist and Hire.',
  'Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role''s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.

## Open a role and send the apply link

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links.

1. Press **Open the role** to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); **Close the role** takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.
2. Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.
3. Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role''s questions, about five minutes.
4. **Pass mark and pay** changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.

