, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens their record. If it is outside your window, opening it from their call is logged as an opening for 24 hours with the reason Incoming call, as <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b> is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the line at the top right of the call to minimize it: it becomes a small chip at the bottom of the page with the caller&#39;s name and the call&#39;s timer. Clicking anywhere outside the panel, or pressing Esc, minimizes it too. Press the chip to open the call again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. A new call always opens by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call helper (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Inside every call on the pop-up, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> tells you what to say and do. It is made for your first weeks; press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> when you no longer need it (<b class="gd-ui">Show</b> brings it back).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Say</b>: the greeting to read out, with your first name, and the caller&#39;s name and booking when we know them. Start every call with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What is the call about?</b> Press the button that fits: New booking or price question, Change or extend a booking, Running late or late return, Pick-up and delivery, Deposit and payments, Insurance and protection, Accident or damage, Complaint, Owner wants to list a car, or Job applicant. You get 3 to 6 short steps. Words in bold quotes are what to say; a link opens the right page of your portal. <b class="gd-ui">All situations</b> goes back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>: type a word (deposit, late, cancel, km) for the short answer to the questions callers ask most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The amounts, days and percentages in the steps and answers come from the settings, so they are always the ones in force. Never quote a price from memory: the offer screen works it out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Always finish with <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin writes the greetings, the steps and the answers. Something wrong or missing? Tell an Admin: they change it in Settings and you see it on the next call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s record (<b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>, then Open) has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and the notes are in its Activity log (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>), newest first, each with the date and time, who wrote it and their role. Add a note for every situation: what they asked, what you told them, what happens next. Notes cannot be changed or removed by staff, so write a new note to correct one; an Admin can remove a note with a reason. The notes also show on the caller pop-up and on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-lanes-the-call-button-and-hidden-numbers-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lanes, the Call button and hidden numbers (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each conversation has a lane: <b class="gd-ui">Fleet</b> for a car on rent, or a pickup, return, delivery or collection within a day; <b class="gd-ui">Customer service</b> for the rest. The inbox has a tab for each. The caller pop-up rings for Fleet first on Fleet&#39;s calls; customer service gets them when no Fleet staff member is on duty or nobody answered within 20 seconds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> places the call in your browser (release 44, below): the customer sees the CarmaCars number, and the call is noted on their history with its length. Until calling from the site is set up, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo as before and says why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sales sees customer numbers hidden, like (647) •••-••00. Use <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> on the page: the number is found on our side. Search by phone still works.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-in-your-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in your browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">You make and take calls in the staff portal, in your browser, on the CarmaCars number. Your own phone number is never used and never shown, wherever you work from.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Use a computer with a headset (or earphones with a microphone) in Chrome, Edge or Safari. The first time you call, the browser asks to use the microphone: press <b class="gd-ui">Allow</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a booking or any staff page. A bar opens at the bottom left of the page (at the top on a phone): <b class="gd-ui">Calling ...</b>, then the call&#39;s timer once they answer. The customer sees the CarmaCars number. Sales: the number stays hidden, the call goes through all the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">During the call: <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> (for a phone menu that asks you to press a number) and <b class="gd-ui">Hang up</b>. Do not close or reload the page during a call: that ends it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Incoming calls: when someone calls the CarmaCars number, your browser rings while a staff page is open (customer service and Sales by default). Press <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. The first person to answer takes the call and the others stop ringing. You see the caller&#39;s name when we know it (Sales: the number hidden).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online, or nobody answers: the caller hears a short message, and it is a missed call with its task, like every missed call. A call is never forwarded to your own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Keep a staff page open during your shift with the computer&#39;s sound on, so you hear the ring.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Something went wrong (the microphone not allowed, the connection lost): the bar says what to do. Press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>, fix it and call again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calling-from-the-site-your-mobile-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calling from the site: your mobile (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a request or a booking rings your own mobile first, then connects the person. They see the CarmaCars number, never yours. Sales see the number hidden and call this way only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The first time, with no mobile on your profile, a small window asks <b class="gd-ui">Your mobile number</b>. Type your Canadian or US mobile (10 digits, for example (647) 555-0123) and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and call</b>. No code is texted: it is saved to your profile and the call starts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your phone rings. Answer it: you hear &quot;CarmaCars call. Connecting you now.&quot; and the person&#39;s phone rings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A call that cannot start says why in the same window, with <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b>. Calling from the site not set up: ask customer service or an Admin to call, and tell an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To add your number as a sign-in, use <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sign-in</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>. No code after a minute? Press <b class="gd-ui">Resend the code</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Save it without a code</b>: calls still ring it, but you sign in with your email until it is verified.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'shared-tools', 'chapter', 'car-maintenance', 'Every function has the calendar and Find a renter. Use them to answer questions fast.

## The calendar

1. Every car with its photo, its bookings, requests and blocks. The red line is now. Tap a bar for its details; on a phone it opens on the agenda, by day.
2. Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by plate, booking or name.
3. Fleet and customer service can remove a cleaning block from its side panel (**Remove the block**) when a car is ready sooner.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 800; address: carmacars.ca/va/calendar; pins: 1 60.2 33.8, 2 28.5 17.5")

## Find a car

**Bookings**, the **Find a car** tab. A renter quotes the car code on the car''s page (like CC-7F3A).

1. Type the car code, a plate, a VIN or the name. Each car shows its code, plate, status and its page on the site.
2. In Add a rental, type the car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.

## Find a renter

1. Search by name, email, phone or booking number.
2. Opening a renter''s private details asks for a reason (**Open with a reason**). It is kept in the access log.
3. The renter''s record has **Add a note** and the **Activity** log: everything about the renter, newest first, with a chip per type (All by default), **Search the activity**, **Older** for the next 50, and **Email**, **Call** and **Text**. Fleet does not see payments in it.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-07-renters-desktop-99cfd0ef.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 240; address: carmacars.ca/va/renters; pins: 1 68.3 34.6")

## Email the renter

Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance can all write to the renter from a booking: press **Email the renter**, or open the **Messages & history** section.

The booking page, the car page and the listing review are the same pages an Admin opens. The car page has the Admin''s tabs your function uses: **Overview**, **Rates & fees** and **Maintenance** (Fleet), **Listing** and **Documents**; an old link to a car''s maintenance opens its Maintenance tab. You see the sections and buttons of your function: Finance has the money, the refunds and the deposit; Fleet the field jobs, the handovers and the car''s rates; customer service the review and offer, changes and extensions; Sales the requests and offers.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from.
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars and the renter can answer in their account; the answer opens a task for customer service.
3. On a booking an insurer pays you can choose Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance) as the sender, and **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster on the booking.

The form is under the booking''s Activity log (release 35), which lists the messages both ways, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes and the rest, newest first, with a chip per type and a search. Each email counts against the daily email limit, shown under the form with today''s number.

### Find a booking
**Bookings**: type at least 3 characters of the booking number (CC-1042, 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number, a plate or a car code, then press Enter. **My bookings** lists yours, with your commission. Every search is logged, as Find a renter.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer for new requests, replies to answer and urgent problems, even with the portal closed.

1. Open **Profile** (top of the menu). Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications. The first page of the portal also offers it once.
2. Under **What to alert me about**: new requests, booking changes and messages are on for staff; payments are off until you tick them.
3. **Send a test alert** checks the device. **Remove** takes an old phone off.

On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**). Use your phone''s own Focus or Do Not Disturb for quiet hours.

### Search

The **Search** button at the top of every page (or press **/** where the page has no search box of its own) finds pages and the records your role may open: bookings and requests by number, renter name, email, phone or plate, renters, owners and cars.

### A VIN from the car

VIN fields have **Scan the barcode** (the barcode in the driver''s door frame or under the windshield) and **Photo of the VIN**. Check what was read against the car before saving.

## Alerts by email

Alerts that are not urgent come together in one email at most once an hour; urgent ones (a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, the site down) still come on their own. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once. Choose on **Profile**, Notifications: alerts by email, **Change how often**: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.

> Tip: To change the email you sign in with, open Profile, Sign-in and press **Change my email**: type the new address, and we send a confirmation link to it and tell the old address. Your email changes only when the link is opened, and every record of yours follows it.', 'Shared tools', 'The calendar and Find a renter.',
  'Every function has the calendar and Find a renter. Use them to answer questions fast.

## Which cars are free (release 44)

At the top of **Calendar**: choose the **Pickup** and the **Return** the customer wants and you see every car at once.

1. Each car says **Available** (green edge) or **Not available** (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the **Next free** start for the same length of rental.
2. An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.
3. Narrow it with **Class**, **Seats at least** and **Price a day up to**, or tick **Available only**.
4. Customer service and Sales: press **Offer these dates** on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.
5. No customer''s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.

## The calendar

1. Every car with its photo, its bookings, requests and blocks, in the colours of the legend above it: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance, block. The red line is now. Tap a bar for its details; on a phone it opens on the agenda, by day.
2. Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by plate, booking or name.
3. Fleet and customer service can remove a cleaning block from its side panel (**Remove the block**) when a car is ready sooner.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 800; address: carmacars.ca/va/calendar; pins: 1 60.2 33.8, 2 28.5 17.5")

