> Tip: To change the email you sign in with, open Profile, Sign-in and press **Change my email**: type the new address, and we send a confirmation link to it and tell the old address. Your email changes only when the link is opened, and every record of yours follows it.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every function has the calendar and Find a renter. Use them to answer questions fast.</p><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-which-cars-are-free-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which cars are free (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Calendar</b>: choose the <b class="gd-ui">Pickup</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Return</b> the customer wants and you see every car at once.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car says <b class="gd-ui">Available</b> (green edge) or <b class="gd-ui">Not available</b> (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the <b class="gd-ui">Next free</b> start for the same length of rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Narrow it with <b class="gd-ui">Class</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Seats at least</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Price a day up to</b>, or tick <b class="gd-ui">Available only</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service and Sales: press <b class="gd-ui">Offer these dates</b> on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No customer&#39;s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-the-calendar" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The calendar</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every car with its photo, its bookings, requests and blocks, in the colours of the legend above it: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance, block. The red line is now. Tap a bar for its details; on a phone it opens on the agenda, by day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by plate, booking or name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet and customer service can remove a cleaning block from its side panel (<b class="gd-ui">Remove the block</b>) when a car is ready sooner.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/calendar</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/800"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="800"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:60.2%;top:33.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:28.5%;top:17.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-find-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> tab. A renter quotes the car code on the car&#39;s page (like CC-7F3A).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the car code, a plate, a VIN or the name. Each car shows its code, plate, status and its page on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">In Add a rental, type the car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Opening a renter&#39;s private details asks for a reason (<b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>). It is kept in the access log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter&#39;s record has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, with a chip per type (All by default), <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> for the next 50, and <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. Fleet does not see payments in it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/renters</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/240"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-07-renters-desktop-99cfd0ef.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="240"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.3%;top:34.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-email-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance can all write to the renter from a booking: press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>, or open the <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section.</p><p class="gd-p">The booking page, the car page and the listing review are the same pages an Admin opens. The car page has the Admin&#39;s tabs your function uses: <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> (Fleet), <b class="gd-ui">Listing</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>; an old link to a car&#39;s maintenance opens its Maintenance tab. You see the sections and buttons of your function: Finance has the money, the refunds and the deposit; Fleet the field jobs, the handovers and the car&#39;s rates; customer service the review and offer, changes and extensions; Sales the requests and offers.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Write a <b class="gd-ui">Subject</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Message</b>, or pick a <b class="gd-ui">Quick reply</b> to start from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>. It goes from CarmaCars and the renter can answer in their account; the answer opens a task for customer service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking an insurer pays you can choose Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance) as the sender, and <b class="gd-ui">Email the adjuster</b> writes to the adjuster on the booking.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The form is under the booking&#39;s Activity log (release 35), which lists the messages both ways, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes and the rest, newest first, with a chip per type and a search. Each email counts against the daily email limit, shown under the form with today&#39;s number.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Find a booking</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>: type at least 3 characters of the booking number (CC-1042, 1042), the renter&#39;s or a driver&#39;s name, an email, a phone number, a plate or a car code, then press Enter. <b class="gd-ui">My bookings</b> lists yours, with your commission. Every search is logged, as Find a renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer for new requests, replies to answer and urgent problems, even with the portal closed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> (top of the menu). Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications. The first page of the portal also offers it once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>: new requests, booking changes and messages are on for staff; payments are off until you tick them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> checks the device. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes an old phone off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>). Use your phone&#39;s own Focus or Do Not Disturb for quiet hours.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Search</h3><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> button at the top of every page (or press <b class="gd-ui">/</b> where the page has no search box of its own) finds pages and the records your role may open: bookings and requests by number, renter name, email, phone or plate, renters, owners and cars.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A VIN from the car</h3><p class="gd-p">VIN fields have <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> (the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or under the windshield) and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Check what was read against the car before saving.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-alerts-by-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alerts by email</h2><p class="gd-p">Alerts that are not urgent come together in one email at most once an hour; urgent ones (a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, the site down) still come on their own. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once. Choose on <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, Notifications: alerts by email, <b class="gd-ui">Change how often</b>: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>To change the email you sign in with, open Profile, Sign-in and press <b class="gd-ui">Change my email</b>: type the new address, and we send a confirmation link to it and tell the old address. Your email changes only when the link is opened, and every record of yours follows it.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'start-here', 'start', null, '### Who this guide is for

CarmaCars field staff: drivers, detailers, and drivers who also detail. You hand cars over, take them back, move them and shoot listing photos. Everything is on your phone. Your jobs are under **Field work** in the staff portal; if you also hold another function (Sales, for example), its pages are in the same menu.

### What you need

- Your phone, charged, with a data connection (photos and signatures save as you take them)
- The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)
- A car charger and a cloth for the camera lens

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email on your phone and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password and press **Save the new password**.
2. You land on **Today**. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in` with your Email and Password.
3. In your browser''s menu, choose **Add to Home Screen**. The portal then opens full screen, like an app.
4. Open **Profile**, add your mobile number and press **Save my phone**.
5. At the top of the page, fill in your Home address and Postal code and press **Save my home address**. You need it before you add a rental or earn a commission.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 4 92.3 78.3")

> Good to know: Recommended: on Profile, press **Set up two-step sign-in** and follow the steps with an authenticator app.

## Stuck on a page?

If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the right chapter in a sheet from the bottom of the screen; **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Open the Academy lesson** opens the lesson in a new tab. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while a renter signs.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: the academy (Training) first, then your staff agreement, then your jobs. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and Today show the team''s WhatsApp group: join it, then press **I joined**.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## Report a bug (release 37)
Something not working? Press **Report a bug** at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (**Blocks my work** alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. **My bug reports** shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won''t fix.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.', 'Start here', 'Who this is for and your first sign-in.',
  '### Who this guide is for

CarmaCars field staff: drivers, detailers, and drivers who also detail. You hand cars over, take them back, move them and shoot listing photos. Everything is on your phone. Your jobs are under **Field work** in the staff portal; if you also hold another function (Sales, for example), its pages are in the same menu.

### What you need

- Your phone, charged, with a data connection (photos and signatures save as you take them)
- The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)
- A car charger and a cloth for the camera lens

## Once you are hired

You are not working a shift right away. First your training (the academy), then you claim your shifts online in the portal.

1. Say hello in the team chat: the CarmaCars Team WhatsApp group (the link is in your portal once the academy and your agreement are done).
2. In each WhatsApp group you are in, set your member tag as "Name - Position", for example "Ali - Field".

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email on your phone and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password and press **Save the new password**.
2. You land on **Today**. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in` with your Email and Password.
3. In your browser''s menu, choose **Add to Home Screen**. The portal then opens full screen, like an app.
4. Open **Profile**, add your mobile number and press **Save my phone**.
5. At the top of the page, fill in your Home address and Postal code and press **Save my home address**. You need it before you add a rental or earn a commission.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 4 92.3 78.3")

> Good to know: Recommended: on Profile, press **Set up two-step sign-in** and follow the steps with an authenticator app.

## Stuck on a page?

If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the right chapter in a sheet from the bottom of the screen; **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Open the Academy lesson** opens the lesson in a new tab. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while a renter signs.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: the academy (Training) first, then your staff agreement, then your jobs. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and Today show the team''s WhatsApp group: join it, then press **I joined**.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## Report a bug (release 37)
Something not working? Press **Report a bug** at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (**Blocks my work** alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. **My bug reports** shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won''t fix.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.',
  '<h3 class="gd-h3">Who this guide is for</h3><p class="gd-p">CarmaCars field staff: drivers, detailers, and drivers who also detail. You hand cars over, take them back, move them and shoot listing photos. Everything is on your phone. Your jobs are under <b class="gd-ui">Field work</b> in the staff portal; if you also hold another function (Sales, for example), its pages are in the same menu.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">What you need</h3><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your phone, charged, with a data connection (photos and signatures save as you take them)</li><li>The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)</li><li>A car charger and a cloth for the camera lens</li></ul><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-once-you-are-hired" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Once you are hired</h2><p class="gd-p">You are not working a shift right away. First your training (the academy), then you claim your shifts online in the portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Say hello in the team chat: the CarmaCars Team WhatsApp group (the link is in your portal once the academy and your agreement are done).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">In each WhatsApp group you are in, set your member tag as &quot;Name - Position&quot;, for example &quot;Ali - Field&quot;.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-your-first-sign-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first sign-in</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the invitation email on your phone and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the new password</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You land on <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>. Next time, sign in at <span class="gd-url